<!--
  ============================================================================
  WildAnimals_Pyrelands.xml                 UtinniPatches — new file 2026-09-13
  ============================================================================

  Wires the RULED fauna roster for the Pyrelands into RM_FE_Pyrelands'
  wildAnimals, replacing the deliberate core-only vanilla placeholder that
  src/RimMandrake/Pyrelands/Defs/BiomeDefs/Pyrelands.xml ships (Hare, Rat,
  Gazelle, Ostrich, Emu, Dromedary, Muffalo, Iguana, Elephant, Rhinoceros,
  Cougar, Fox_Fennec, Warg — kept there so the Pyrelands mod is self-contained
  and works with nothing else loaded). The wiring lives HERE, in UtinniPatches,
  never in the Pyrelands mod itself — that mod must stay standalone.

  🔑 SOURCE OF TRUTH: every defName and every commonality number below is
  copied verbatim from design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/rosters/
  the_pyrelands.json's "fauna" array (authored 2026-09-09, owner-ruled sitting
  entries through 2026-09-10 — the GR_ correction pass, the
  PYRELANDS_FIRE_WEB_COMMISSION_1 igniter builds, and the round-2 move-mapping
  import of Dalgo) — NOT re-derived or rescaled here. That JSON
  is the actual ruling; this file only wires it into the def the game reads.
  The 13-animal sum is 4.41, not the placeholder's ~5.8 — a deliberate
  consequence of using the owner's real per-species numbers rather than
  matching the placeholder's total.

  🔴 2026-09-14 (BOOMALOPE_CUT_EVERYWHERE_1): vanilla Boomalope, originally
  wired here 2026-09-13 under the 2026-09-09 KEEP-reskinned card, is cut —
  owner ruling "Absolutely no boomalopes," reversing that card. Removed from
  the unconditional block and the roster below; counts corrected to 14/4.21.

  🔴 2026-09-14 (BOOMSNAKE_CUT_CONFLICT_1): GR_Boomsnake's ThingDef was cut by
  BOOM_FAMILY_CUT_1 (2026-09-10, 12:48 local) — its presence here traced to a
  round-2 move-mapping decision recorded at 06:20 local the same day, BEFORE
  the cut, mechanically re-applied into the_pyrelands.json by ROSTER_MOVE_APPLY_1
  at 23:59 that same night despite design/Jawa/worldbuilding/review/round2/
  biome_findings.md already recording (07:41 and again 17:45 local, hours
  earlier) that "GR_Boomsnake's 'Pyrelands' move is voided by the boom-family
  cut." No ruling ever restored it — the "GR_ correction pass" cited above
  restored GR_Mantistanis (see its own roster "law" field), not GR_Boomsnake.
  Removed from the Vanilla Genetics Expanded block and the roster below;
  counts corrected to 13/3.71. Fire-follower niche stays AA_Razorjack's, per
  the same day's recast.

  🔑 STRUCTURE: one PatchOperationConditional-guarded PatchOperationReplace
  swaps the WHOLE node for the two commissioned igniters (both always
  loaded — this mod's own defs) — no PatchOperationFindMod needed for
  either. Three more PatchOperationFindMod blocks then splice each donor mod's animals
  in via PatchOperationAdd on the now-existing node, shorthand-dictionary form
  throughout — the whole biome's own wildAnimals list already uses that form
  (`<Hare>1.2</Hare>` etc.), and it is the ONLY form
  BiomeAnimalRecord.LoadDataFromXmlCustom reads (same mechanism as
  WeatherCommonalityRecord — see this mod's AshStorms_Pyrelands.xml for the
  measured citation). A mod that is not loaded means its PatchOperationFindMod
  block simply never fires — no error, no silent wrong-parse.

  ⚠️ A patch that matches nothing logs nothing (PatchOperationFindMod returns
  true on no match of its ops) — validated with
  skills/rimworld-modding/scripts/validate_patch.py against the live def dump
  and the full 590-mod set; see the file-level record for the verdict.

  ============================================================================
  ROSTER AND VERIFICATION
  ============================================================================

  UNCONDITIONAL (this mod's own defs — always loaded):
    RUT_FireHawk       0.15  igniter-flier      — RUT_PyrelandsFauna.xml (this mod)
    RUT_FurnaceBeast   0.08  igniter-megafauna  — RUT_PyrelandsFauna.xml (this mod)

  Alpha Animals (mod name string "Alpha Animals", packageId sarg.alphaanimals
  — confirmed active in ModsConfig.xml). All three defNames verified directly
  against the mod's own shipped XML, Steam Workshop content id 1541721856,
  1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Races/:
    AA_Razorjack       0.20  fire-follower      — Races_Razorjack.xml:5,157
    AA_Barbslinger     0.15  ash-grazer         — Races_BarbSlinger.xml:5,135
    AA_FireWasp        0.40  small-predator     — Races_FireWasp.xml:4,124

  Vanilla Genetics Expanded (mod name string "Vanilla Genetics Expanded",
  packageId VanillaExpanded.VGeneticsE / vanillaexpanded.vgeneticse in
  ModsConfig.xml — confirmed active). Both defNames verified directly against
  the mod's own shipped XML, Steam Workshop content id 2801160906 (About.xml:
  <packageId>VanillaExpanded.VGeneticsE</packageId>, <name>Vanilla Genetics
  Expanded</name>):
    GR_Mantistanis     0.05  large-predator
        — 1.6/Mods/Megafauna/Defs/ThingDefs_Races/Races_Animal_Megafaunahybrids.xml:570
          (ThingDef) and :716 (PawnKindDef).
    NOTE: this download's top-level folder is internally named "Megafauna"
    for the hybrid-animal half of the mod's content — that is this mod's own
    packaging choice, not a sign these defNames belong to the separate,
    RETIRED "Megafauna" workshop mod (AnimalBiomeDuplicates_Fix.xml's header,
    2026-09-05 retirements). Checked: the retired Megafauna mod is not present
    in the active ModsConfig.xml list; Vanilla Genetics Expanded is.

  Star Wars Animal Collection (Continued) (mod name string "Star Wars Animal
  Collection (Continued)", packageId mlie.starwarsanimalcollection — confirmed
  active in ModsConfig.xml). This mod's own workshop download was not present
  in the local Steam Workshop cache to cite a raw XML line directly (only a
  dependent mod, "Star Wars : The Force Standalone", id 3557220601, was found,
  and it does not itself declare these races). Verified instead via TWO
  independent lines of evidence that both require these exact defNames to be
  real, loaded PawnKindDefs sourced from this mod:
    (a) design/Jawa/fauna/animal_census.csv:487,493,515,549,583,585,637 —
        Gizka/Anooba/Dalgo/Iriaz/Nuna/Orray/Zeer, each row's `mod`/`packageId`
        columns naming this exact mod, built from a live per-mod XML scan.
    (b) src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Patches/AnimalBiomeDuplicates_Fix.xml —
        this repo's OWN live fix, confirmed firing against a real capture, for
        `/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_Grasslands"]/wildAnimals/Iriaz[2]`
        (that file's op #40) and (per that file's header) prior removals for
        Gizka/Nuna/Orray/Zeer duplicate records against the same biome — a
        PatchOperationConditional that fires proves the exact node existed in
        the loaded def set, not merely in this mod's own claim.
    Anooba is the bare "Anooba" defName from Star Wars Animal Collection
    (Continued), NOT this repo's own RSW_Anooba port
    (src/RimStarWars/SWBestiary/Defs/ThingDefs_Races/RSW_Anooba.xml) — that
    port is a distinct def created only to resolve a ZBiome_Grasslands/
    Ashkarr duplicate-record collision and is not wired to any other biome by
    that change.
    Anooba              0.35  medium-predator
    Iriaz               0.50  small-herd
    Nuna                0.50  small
    Orray               0.25  medium (burrower + predator double role)
    Zeer                0.60  large-herd
    Dalgo               0.18  brake (round-2 import)
    Gizka               1.00  grain (ECOSYSTEM_PYRAMID_LAW_1: the most-seen animal)

  ============================================================================
  LEFT OUT: vanilla Boomalope (BOOMALOPE_CUT_EVERYWHERE_1, 2026-09-14 — see
  above) and GR_Boomsnake (BOOMSNAKE_CUT_CONFLICT_1, 2026-09-14 — see above;
  its ThingDef is Cherry-Picker cut by BOOM_FAMILY_CUT_1 and no ruling ever
  restored it). Every other name in the item's checklist resolved to a real
  defName in a real, active mod — RUT_FireHawk, RUT_FurnaceBeast, AA_Razorjack,
  AA_Barbslinger, AA_FireWasp, GR_Mantistanis, Anooba, Iriaz,
  Nuna, Orray, Zeer, Dalgo. One more name not in the item's own checklist but
  present in the_pyrelands.json's ruled "fauna" array — Gizka — is wired too,
  because the item's brief was to wire "the ruled fauna roster" and the JSON
  is that roster; leaving it out would silently under-wire a roster the owner
  already ruled complete. GR_Mantistanis looked riskiest at first (its
  defining XML sits inside a workshop download whose internal folder is
  named "Megafauna") but resolved cleanly: see the Megafauna-folder note above.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- Always: replace the vanilla core-only placeholder with the two
       commissioned igniters plus vanilla Boomalope. Unconditional on any
       DONOR mod — all three defNames are this mod's own or Core, always
       loaded whenever UtinniPatches is — but still PatchOperationConditional-
       guarded on the target node itself, so this becomes a silent no-op
       rather than a red launch error in the (currently impossible, but not
       worth risking) case that the Pyrelands mod is ever removed while
       UtinniPatches stays in. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FE_Pyrelands"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FE_Pyrelands"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
      <value>
        <wildAnimals>
          <RUT_FireHawk>0.15</RUT_FireHawk>
          <RUT_FurnaceBeast>0.08</RUT_FurnaceBeast>
        </wildAnimals>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- Alpha Animals: fire-follower predator, ash-grazer, and the small
       fire-armed native. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Alpha Animals</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FE_Pyrelands"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
      <value>
        <AA_Razorjack>0.2</AA_Razorjack>
        <AA_Barbslinger>0.15</AA_Barbslinger>
        <AA_FireWasp>0.4</AA_FireWasp>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- Vanilla Genetics Expanded: fire-follower predator hybrid. GR_Boomsnake
       removed 2026-09-14 (BOOMSNAKE_CUT_CONFLICT_1) — its ThingDef is
       Cherry-Picker cut by BOOM_FAMILY_CUT_1; no ruling ever restored it. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Vanilla Genetics Expanded</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FE_Pyrelands"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
      <value>
        <GR_Mantistanis>0.05</GR_Mantistanis>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- Star Wars Animal Collection (Continued): the SW-canon herd, Anooba as
       a second flame-edge hunter, and Gizka as the quick grain-forager. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Star Wars Animal Collection (Continued)</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FE_Pyrelands"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
      <value>
        <Anooba>0.35</Anooba>
        <Iriaz>0.5</Iriaz>
        <Nuna>0.5</Nuna>
        <Orray>0.25</Orray>
        <Zeer>0.6</Zeer>
        <Dalgo>0.18</Dalgo>
        <Gizka>1.0</Gizka>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
